item.text:
[
  {
    "task_id": "ctx-k2-2",
    "params": {
      "keysel": [0, 0, 9, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0],
      "bg": [9, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]
    },
    "rationale": "Use own colour and the column's nonzero colour set. In demonstration 1, columns with set {1,2} map 1 and 2 to 8, while columns with set {2,3} map 3 to 9. Demonstration 5 also maps zeros to 3 in the column whose set is {1}."
  },
  {
    "task_id": "ctx-k2-3",
    "params": {
      "keysel": [0, 0, 9, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0],
      "bg": [9, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]
    },
    "rationale": "Column sets determine the substitutions: {1,2,3} maps 0 to 8 and 2 to 7, as in demonstration 1's second column; {2,3} maps 2 to 0, as in demonstration 2's second column; {1,3} maps 0 to 5, as in demonstration 6's last column."
  },
  {
    "task_id": "ctx-k2-0",
    "params": {
      "keysel": [0, 0, 9, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0],
      "bg": [9, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]
    },
    "rationale": "Use column colour sets excluding 0. Demonstration 1 maps 0 to 2 in {1,3} columns. Demonstration 2 maps 2 to 9 in its {1,2} column. Demonstration 3's {1,2,3} first column maps 0 to 2 and 1 to 0."
  },
  {
    "task_id": "ctx-k0-1",
    "params": {
      "keysel": [9, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0],
      "bg": [9, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]
    },
    "rationale": "Use the complete 3x3 neighbourhood including boundary padding. Demonstrations 4 and 5 change a top-left 0 to 6 when its right, lower, and lower-right neighbours are all 0. Demonstration 7 changes the top-right 1 to 9 with its three in-grid neighbours all 0."
  },
  {
    "task_id": "ctx-k0-2",
    "params": {
      "keysel": [9, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0],
      "bg": [9, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]
    },
    "rationale": "The full padded 3x3 pattern distinguishes the sole change: demonstration 8 changes its top-right 0 to 4, where the left, lower-left, and lower neighbours are all 0. Other demonstrated neighbourhoods retain their centre colours."
  },
  {
    "task_id": "ctx-k2-1",
    "params": {
      "keysel": [0, 0, 9, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0],
      "bg": [9, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]
    },
    "rationale": "Use own colour plus the nonzero column set. Demonstration 1 maps 0 to 9 for set {3}, 0 to 4 for {1,3}, and both 0 and 3 to 6 for {1,2,3}. Demonstration 3 leaves its other column sets unchanged."
  },
  {
    "task_id": "ctx-k6-1",
    "params": {
      "keysel": [0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 9, 0],
      "bg": [9, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]
    },
    "rationale": "Use directional nearest nonzero colours. Demonstration 1's top-right 0 becomes 9 with no colour above or right, 3 below, and 2 left. Demonstration 8's first three zeros become 5 with no colour above or left, 3 below, and 1 right."
  },
  {
    "task_id": "ctx-k0-3",
    "params": {
      "keysel": [9, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0],
      "bg": [9, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]
    },
    "rationale": "Use the full padded 3x3 pattern. Demonstration 5 changes row 4, column 7 from 0 to 2: its neighbourhood has two all-zero in-grid columns and an out-of-grid right column. All other demonstrated patterns preserve their centres."
  },
  {
    "task_id": "ctx-k5-1",
    "params": {
      "keysel": [0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 9, 0, 0],
      "bg": [9, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]
    },
    "rationale": "Own colour and border status exactly express the rule. Demonstration 1 maps border colours 0,1,2,3 to 5,6,1,9 respectively, while its interior colours remain unchanged; the remaining demonstrations repeat this border mapping."
  },
  {
    "task_id": "ctx-k3-3",
    "params": {
      "keysel": [0, 0, 0, 9, 0, 0, 0, 0],
      "bg": [9, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]
    },
    "rationale": "Use own colour with both nonzero row and column sets. Demonstration 4 maps 0 to 4 for row set {1,2} and column set {2,3}, and 2 to 4 for row set {1,2,3} and column set {2,3}. Demonstration 7 maps 0 to 9 for row set {1} and column set {1,2,3}; demonstration 9 maps 2 to 3 when both sets are {1,2,3}."
  }
]
